Graded Forecast: the market's level, the kind of line and the hold instead of the dip rank

The Chance is read from the market's level (green / amber / red), the line's cell (era, the three rules, busy or
thin, new card, CGC) and the hold; it is shown with its range and never above 85%. The dip rank no longer scores
or orders a slab: Best to Buy is Chance, then a tie-breaker, then price; an extended line carries a warning; a
line whose era has run beyond anything in the history gets no Chance. Recording's Rank column is Line. The phone
app reads the same data. History's replay and Spotcheck still run the model before this one (said on the page).
The raw tab is not touched.

